<http://data.silknow.org/object/67030f72-900a-3656-966a-6d143a78f415/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Shawl. Pale buff-coloured silk crepe ground embroidered with twisted coloured silks in satin stitch ( purple, green, pink, orange, grey, black and white). The shawl is embroidered at both sides. Long fringe at all sides. There is a wide inner border, filled with water and landscape scenes, wherein appear buildings, human figures variously employed (rowing, walking, playing etc.) deer, birds and butterflies; there is an outer narrow border with a variety of floral stems. In the inner corners are four groups of flowering plants (the peony, the magnolia and the narcissus), each group is practically a repetition of the others. 1800-1850"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/67030f72-900a-3656-966a-6d143a78f415> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/67030f72-900a-3656-966a-6d143a78f415>
